# Shiprate Project rules

## Scope

Shiprate feature work belongs to the **Shiprate Enforcer** Cursor Project. Read Project Context before large changes; this repo mirrors workflow docs in `docs/agent-workflow.md`.

## Execution

- Default: **self-hosted Mac** worker on this checkout (`~/Projects/shiprate-enforcer`).
- **Builder** implements; **Tester** verifies with a **different model** than Builder.
- Do not claim a slice done without test sign-off per `docs/testing.md`.

## Context (read first)

- `docs/shiprate-mvp-spec.md` — MVP scope and invariants
- `docs/partner-variable-sheet.md`, `docs/etl-drop-contract.md`, `docs/wizard-field-lists.md`
- `docs/testing.md` — pytest, Playwright, CI parity

## Hard product rules

- Money in **minor units**; rating engine is authoritative.
- **No auto-send** dispute emails; drafts and human approval only.
- **AI** assists column mapping only; it does not rate shipments or submit disputes.
- **RLS:** respect tenant boundaries; never bypass org context in API or tests.

## Edward-facing UX

When giving Edward instructions in this repo, follow `.cursor/rules/how-we-work.mdc` (one step, plain English).
